@startuml correction-sharded-routing
' How the shared T_lex ∘ T_gram beam scores over a SHARDED corpus: each n-gram lookup
' routes (first-token, order) by the importer's own pure function, opens that one shard
' READ-ONLY (never create/evict/checkpoint), and views it as u64 n-grams; an absent
' first-token yields None ⟹ "no n-gram evidence" (count 0). Anchored vs fanout neighbors.
' Second branch (M5): at an EMPTY history (boundary-less sentence start, bos_id = None) the
' successor oracle needs every stored first-token — the single store reads its whole-view
' root edges, the sharded store fans out over EVERY shard root and de-dups; the two return
' the SAME unigram set (parity), both feeding the SAME bridge filter / insertion arm.
' Colour: slate = observed input / one physical shard; purple = the shared pure router /
'   successor seam (the seam that makes storage and query co-locate); teal = read-only
'   coordinator open and the u64 count-store view / root enumeration; blue = the shared
'   GrammarCore beam decoder and the parity join; muted grey = the absent-shard "no
'   evidence" branch.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/correction-sharded-routing.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 6 in docs/integration/lling-llang/hierarchical-correction.md §6.9
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title ShardedView — n-gram lookup (route ⟶ open read-only ⟶ view)  +  empty-history successor fan-out,  feeding the shared GrammarCore beam

rectangle "**observed n-gram**\n[w₀, w₁, …]   ·   first-token w₀,  order = key_len" as ng #455A64

rectangle "**compute_shard_key_from_token(w₀, order, granularity)**\nhash(w₀) mod num_shards   —or—   prefix(w₀, order)\nthe SAME pure fn the importer's route_tokens used to STORE  ⟹  co-location" as route #6A1B9A

rectangle "**ShardCoordinator::get_shard_readonly(key)**\nresident-or-open  ·  open-only\nno create · no evict · no checkpoint   (write-free)" as open #00838F

rectangle "**U64NgramView**  over one shard trie\nSharedARTrie<u64> · trie_arc() clone · lock-free &self reads\nUnit = u64: collapses one LEB128 varint (term-id) per step" as view #00838F

rectangle "**shared GrammarCore beam**   (the identical decoder)\ncount · successor oracle · grammar_neighbors  ⟵ read from THIS shard\nŵ = argmin_w  c_lex + c_gram + λ·(−log S)" as beam #1565C0

rectangle "**Ok(None)** — absent first-token\nno shard file  ⟹  **count 0 / no n-gram evidence**" as none #90A4AE

ng    --> route : (w₀, order)
route --> open  : ShardKey
open  --> view  : Some(shard)
open  --> none  : shard file absent
view  --> beam  : u64 n-gram view
none  --> beam  : no evidence

' ── M5: empty-history successor oracle — first-position insertion at PARITY ──
rectangle "**successors(ε)**  —  EMPTY history\nboundary-less sentence start  ·  bos_id = None\nfirst-position insertion needs every stored first-token (unigram)" as succ #6A1B9A

rectangle "**single store**\nwhole_view().root().edges()" as sroot #00838F
rectangle "**sharded**  all_shards_root_successors\ndiscover_shard_files + get_shard_readonly\nfan out over EVERY shard root  ·  de-dup" as xroot #00838F

rectangle "**same unigram set — PARITY**\n⟶ bridge filter ⟶ insertion arm of the beam" as parity #1565C0

succ   --> sroot  : SingleView (default)
succ   --> xroot  : ShardedView (override)
sroot  --> parity : root edge ids
xroot  --> parity : root edge ids   (≡ single)
parity --> beam   : bridged successors

note right of open #E3F2FD
  Adaptive-granularity caveat: route by the PRODUCED length —
  |h|+1 for the successor oracle, not the history length —
  exactly as route_tokens(tokens) used order = |tokens| at storage time.
  whole_view() = None: unigrams span every shard, so there is no
  single whole-store view — it now backs only the degenerate empty-sequence
  grammar_neighbors query; first-position insertion is served at parity by the
  successors fan-out (below).
end note

legend bottom
  |= neighbor query |= shards walked |= use |
  | **grammar_neighbors**  (anchored, default) | the query's OWN first-token / length shard | decode hot path — co-located continuations, what the beam relies on |
  | **grammar_neighbors_fanout** | EVERY shard, merged (min distance, max frequency) | batch / offline — restores first-token-edit completeness |
endlegend
@enduml
